  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Admission and state",
      "items": [
        "Authentication reads the persistent ledger. Quotas use separate vector/cache Redis. Body/deadline/concurrency limits precede generation. Runtime ACLs cannot administer keys or budgets. Sources: internal/application/application.go:268\u2013314; cmd/deployment-init/main.go:96\u2013105.",
        "Compose pins images, enables private TLS/ACL connections, separates volumes and sets memory/CPU limits. /ready checks ledger and both Search indexes; no provider call. Sources: docker-compose.yml:1\u201391; internal/application/application.go:301\u2013310."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Retrieval and reuse",
      "items": [
        "Project-filtered RAG and cache each embed the question; cache hits avoid chat but retain embedding charges. Ordinary errors allow ungrounded work; budget errors reject. Sources: internal/completion/completion.go:137\u2013183; internal/cache/embeddings.go:54\u2013136.",
        "Cache scope includes project, primary route, schema, corpus revision and prompt-policy-v1. Complete fallback answers keep that namespace; each paid attempt has its own charge. Sources: internal/completion/completion.go:167\u2013181,223\u2013270; internal/cache/namespace.go:22\u201335."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Prompt and provider boundaries",
      "items": [
        "Fixed system policy, JSON-encoded references, and separate user question share one builder across JSON/SSE/fallback. No tools, classifier, phrase blocklist, or output screening. Sources: internal/completion/input.go:5\u201343; internal/provider/openai.go:64\u2013104.",
        "JSON/error reads: 1 MiB; embedding reads: 128 KiB; SSE: 4 MiB cumulative, 1 MiB per line. Oversized or incomplete responses never produce successful cache entries. Sources: internal/provider/openai.go:16\u201328,164\u2013194; internal/cache/embeddings.go:110\u2013136; internal/completion/stream.go:172\u2013227."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Financial lifecycle",
      "items": [
        "Reserve before every chat/embedding call. Defaults: 100,000 tokens and US$10/project/UTC day. Integer nanodollars; immutable event IDs; unknown outcomes retain full reservations. Source: internal/usage/tracker.go:16\u201317,78\u2013174.",
        "Provider usage settles known work. Abandonment records labelled estimates, preserves holds and closes upstream. Detached settlement: 5s. Explicit operator reconciliation appends evidence; audit repairs only validated aggregate snapshots. Sources: internal/completion/metered.go:33\u201343,137\u2013169; internal/usage/reconcile.go:84\u2013155,259\u2013345."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Operators and honest evidence",
      "items": [
        "project-key preserves binding, adds 90-day new expiry and 24h default overlap. Explicit key/usage migration preserves old records and totals. Backup/isolated restore scripts verify synthetic RDB/AOF recovery. Sources: cmd/project-key/main.go:24\u201391; internal/auth/migration.go:94\u2013146; internal/usage/reconcile.go:165\u2013235; scripts/ledger-restore-check.sh:1\u2013128.",
        "Smoke/cache/adversarial tools are opt-in. Adversarial default prepares an unpaid report: fixed controls, three trials per JSON/SSE case. No paid/live resistance or invoice evidence measured. Sources: cmd/adversarial-eval/main.go:49\u2013161; docs/evaluation/adversarial-prepared-v1.md:1\u201313."
      ]
    }
  ]
